Package: DataFlow
Title: Publication-Quality Study-Design Flow Diagrams
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("batestguy", email = "batesthommie@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Build study-design flow diagrams (sampling, clustering,
    selection, assignment, splits, exclusions and merges) with a small set of
    pipe-friendly verbs, and draw them as 'ggplot2' graphics for publication.
    Counts are drawn exactly as typed; they are never computed or checked.
    Every diagram also has a plain-language written description for use as
    alternative text.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports:
    ggplot2 (>= 3.5.0),
    grDevices,
    stats,
    grid,
    utils
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    vdiffr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.1
